# What comes next

The accepted package contains 10 full essays for reading. The 22-candidate preparation and this reading selection are complete within their recorded scope.

1. Use the [packet](reading/20261018/README.md), which omits grades and selection labels, as the fixed input for the next checks. On October 31 the custodian preferred a short decision summary to reading all ten; AI-led verification followed by five short candidate cards is proposed, not yet launched.
2. Check the strongest arguments, closest prior work, quotations, and unresolved objections using the exact selected versions.
3. Choose three essays and two reserves. Independently check any later substantive changes.
4. Prepare manuscripts and the methodology report against the then-current submission rules. Submit only on an explicit instruction.

There is no fixed calendar or prescribed division into chats. Completed campaigns remain closed. Original essays, earlier versions, rejected candidates, disagreements, and retained logs remain part of the record.

Completion is bounded to the accepted package. Earlier capture gaps remain in the record; this is not a claim that the complete history of either provider was captured. Exact visible fragments preserve selected text and its source hashes without exporting full native envelopes or hidden reasoning.

Public release remains a separate decision under the [publication policy](PUBLICATION.md).
